            <ArticleTitle>What Is the Role of the Bacterium Propionibacterium acnes in Type 1 Modic Changes? A Review of the Literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>419-424</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0846-5371(17)30104-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carj.2017.07.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review presents a summary of the pathology and epidemiology of Modic changes and the possible role of Propionibacterium acnes. This information is followed by a synthesis of the most recent clinical research involved in culturing the discs of patients with degenerative disc disease for the presence of bacteria. We also discuss a randomized controlled trial that investigates the effects of antibiotics on patients with chronic low back pain and type 1 Modic changes. We conclude with a brief discussion of the difficulties involved in this research and the significance of the findings.</AbstractText>
